    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d238-a1">

                <pb facs="0637" n="609" sameAs="frus:frus1945-50Intel/pg609"/>

                <head>Attachment<anchor n="1" xml:id="d238-f1"/></head>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#bold">Letter From Acting Secretary of State Lovett to the Director of the Bureau of the
                        Budget (Webb)</hi>
                </p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Webb</hi>: The Department has received your letter of
                    December 24,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d238-f2"/> in which comment is requested by
                    the Bureau of the Budget on the “Proposed Central Intelligence Act of 1949”
                    admitted by the Central Intelligence Agency.</p>
                <pb facs="0638" n="610" xml:id="pg610"/>
                <p>The Department perceives no objection to this proposed legislation. You will note
                    that one clause, 6(g), has been revised in consultation with CIA, according to
                    the attachment. </p>
                <p>The Department believes that despite the extraordinary grant of powers involved,
                    such legislation is entirely proper and necessary for the efficient operation of
                    an intelligence service. </p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,<anchor n="3" xml:id="d238-f3"/></p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
